  "id": "b1646904-04b3-4f37-937f-ed85dfcd9018",
  "title": "Unified Diffusion Models and EEG Representation Techniques",
  "summary": "This paper presents a systematic analysis of diffusion components, introducing DUNE (Diffusion Unified Network Refiner) to detect and suppress artifacts in deep low-noise internal latents, with experiments across multiple backbones showing improved fidelity and reduced hallucinations. DiffEEG, a self-supervised foundation model, addresses EEG seizure detection challenges through denoising diffusion pre-training and RL-based fine-tuning.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The first report introduces DUNE (Diffusion Unified Network Refiner) to refine diffusion models, achieving improved fidelity and reduced hallucinations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The second report presents DiffEEG, a 9.6M-parameter model with U-Net architecture, achieving 61% accuracy in seizure subtyping and 81% accuracy in binary detection.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both studies demonstrate strong architectural capacity and clinical viability for EEG-based seizure monitoring.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
